## What this session accomplished

**Infrastructure recovery** (clyde had been rebooted): rebuilt the SCST target with both multipath portals, booted all 32 VMs, restored the passfile and 2-path mpatha on every node, and confirmed the board state: 1/2/4/8/16/caw all 17/17 PASS, 32/caw 16/17 with only dir_reuse_coherency pending.

**One proven root-cause fix (v0.10.34)**: the cluster-killing failure was a release-fence wedge — `rm -rf` frees dir/bmbt blocks whose mxfs "committed-but-unwritten" accounting survives the free; when dir_reuse reallocates the daddr, the fence finds an unwritable corpse, spins 240s holding the dir EX (P97 shutdown), and 14 peers starve to death. Fixed by retiring the undestaged accounting in `xfs_trans_binval`; the P3B probe caught it firing exactly as predicted and that failure mode has not recurred.

**Pace war** (RULE 0: rounds must average ≤186s; they were ~250-280s): instrumented decomposition showed rm spending 45ms per unlink BAST-stripping up to 31 lingering stat-PR holders per file. The winning combination measured so far: dir-EX-BAST sweep (peers mass-release idle file PRs the moment a held dir is taken by a writer — rm dropped 176s→39s) + acquirer fast-poll + fair handoff, giving 100-147s rounds. Two refuted approaches (per-stat timer reaper; fastpoll-off) were reverted/parameterized with evidence recorded.

**Two remaining bugs identified with full forensics**, fix for the first built but unrun: (1) fair-handoff starves PR waiters behind endless EX rotations (verify's readdir starved 240s → shutdown) — fixed by an `ex_grant_streak` counter in the slot that yields one turn to the whole shared class every 3 EX grants (build `B7A8BCAB`, ready); (2) a genuine dir-coherency corruption (`xfs_dir2_data_use_free`, stale bestfree/leaf image) reproduced once at round-2 create — the old 8-node family reopened at 32, forensics captured.

**Next step** (memory `AAA-ccloopa864-sess1-END-streak-fairness-built-next-run-B2`): sweep/power-cycle the nodes, launch run B2 on build B7A8BCAB with `dirwr=1 dirland=1 close_release=0 caw_inode_fastpoll=1 caw_fair_handoff=1`, and watch for starvation, the use_free corruption, and round pace. The cluster runs are killed, the run lock is free, and the tree builds clean.

